## Building Your Frontend

```
Talent Prism is frontend-agnostic.

The reference implementation demonstrates the complete applicant processing pipeline, but it does not prescribe how organizations should present or consume the resulting data.

You are free to build any interface that best fits your existing technology stack and operational workflows.
```

### Example Frontend Technologies

```
• Retool
• React
• Next.js
• Vue
• Angular
• Bubble
• FlutterFlow
• Lovable
• Internal CRM
• Existing Talent Management Platform
• Custom Admin Dashboard
```

---

## Integrating with Existing Systems

```
Organizations that already operate a talent management system do not need to replace it.

Talent Prism can serve as an AI-powered intake and evaluation layer, with applicant data and evaluation results synchronized into existing platforms after processing.
```

Possible destinations include:

```
• Talent Management System
• Agency CRM
• Internal Database
• Spreadsheet (Excel / Google Sheets)
• Airtable
• Supabase
• PostgreSQL
• Data Warehouse
• Business Intelligence Platform
• Internal APIs
```

---

## Consuming Evaluation Results

```
After processing completes, Talent Prism produces structured evaluation data that can be consumed by downstream applications.

Examples include:

• Structural scores
• Visual assessment
• Agency fit categories
• Confidence scores
• Photo quality assessment
• Applicant metadata
• Processing status
```

Organizations may:

- Display results in a recruiter dashboard
- Synchronize results with an existing talent management platform
- Export results to spreadsheets
- Build custom reporting
- Feed the data into internal automation or analytics systems

